The viewset now adds `DestroyModelMixin` (a DELETE operation) but sets no `permission_classes` or `authentication_classes`, and the `Stream` model's `default_permissions` is `["change", "delete", "view"]` — there is no `add` permission and no explicit permission enforcement on the viewset. The new DELETE endpoint therefore relies on DRF defaults with no object-level ownership/permission check, exposing a missing-authorization surface for the newly added destructive operation.

