The change only sets the JWT `typ` header to the standard SSF value `secevent+jwt` when signing Security Event Tokens. This is a token-encoding/signing detail, not an authorization decision. There is no user-controlled identifier, no missing/incorrect role check, and no policy rule violated. No authorization flaw is introduced.

